{"nodes": [{"id": "recovered_handoff_54_handoff_54", "label": "HANDOFF-54 \u2014 The Method 1.6, chat 101 \u2192 chat 102", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "recovered/HANDOFF-54.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Written at a closed section read so the next chat opens on a measured state rather than a carried one; line numbers, counts and heading lists are deliberately re-measured each chat."}, {"id": "recovered_handoff_54_gate_py", "label": "gate.py \u2014 the \u00a70 gate runner", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/HANDOFF-54.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The gate is itself a seated member, so only the bootstrap decode/extract step runs outside it; every step is its own tool call under timeout 280 and any FAIL stops the chat."}, {"id": "recovered_handoff_54_close_py", "label": "close.py \u2014 the guarded compendia close", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/HANDOFF-54.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Must print 'reverse recovers md5 \u2026 == old: True' before writing, so a build that cannot be reversed to the old bundle writes nothing; append-only members are grown with --append, never reseated."}, {"id": "recovered_handoff_54_r2lib", "label": "r2lib \u2014 the shared resolver library (heading_line, section_span, has_token, enclosing)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/HANDOFF-54.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Instruments import it by path and copy nothing, so a resolver fault is fixed in one place; resolvers take the LINE LIST, not the member text."}, {"id": "recovered_handoff_54_build90_main", "label": "BUILD90 main-and-register bundle (md5 49065309b0c4fe8e055f693aed295cca)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/HANDOFF-54.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Unchanged since chat 62 because the chat-67 hold forbids Register entries."}, {"id": "recovered_handoff_54_build130_compendia", "label": "BUILD130 compendia/papers/audits bundle (md5 16b9f2c4c495cca4a8c03bda939861e4)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/HANDOFF-54.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "recovered_handoff_54_rulings_r2", "label": "RULINGS-R2.md, chat-95 block \u2014 a finding is not a question", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "recovered/HANDOFF-54.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A deviation in the mathematics or the prose is recorded and flagged for repair, never put to M; only a choice no file can settle reaches the author."}, {"id": "recovered_handoff_54_deferred_md", "label": "DEFERRED.md \u2014 the cross-chapter deferral blocks", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/HANDOFF-54.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "recovered_handoff_54_repair_docket", "label": "The repair docket carried to R3", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/HANDOFF-54.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Carried forward until R3 executes it and none of it goes to M, so findings accumulate as classes rather than as ad-hoc edits."}, {"id": "recovered_handoff_54_finding_14v_01", "label": "14v-01 \u2014 the false universal of entry stage (six sequences enter above the first ion, Fe at XV)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/HANDOFF-54.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "recovered_handoff_54_finding_14v_02", "label": "14v-02 \u2014 the absent-member class: no C IV row beside C I, C II, C III and C V", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/HANDOFF-54.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "recovered_handoff_54_finding_14v_03", "label": "14v-03 \u2014 the sodium-like column reproduces in shape and in no digit", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/HANDOFF-54.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "recovered_handoff_54_finding_14v_08", "label": "14v-08 \u2014 D is member-dependent and \u00a724.12 does not say which member", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/HANDOFF-54.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "recovered_handoff_54_channel_table", "label": "The Spectra Compendium channel table (section II, L293\u2013L934, totals at L900)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/HANDOFF-54.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "596 rows across 28 elements and 2,269 interior cells; it is the arbiter for every species figure, and the column headed 'fits' actually holds the ionisation stage."}, {"id": "recovered_handoff_54_prints_and_proofs", "label": "The Prints & Proofs original (738,550 B, md5 49900cf41f818ab789bb90fc596ac977)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/HANDOFF-54.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The authentication baseline under Ruling 56: it separates an authoring gap in the input from a production loss in the build."}, {"id": "recovered_handoff_54_r2_ch14v", "label": "r2-ch14v / r2-ch14w \u2014 chat 101's instrument pair", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/HANDOFF-54.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "recovered_handoff_54_r2_ch14x", "label": "r2-ch14x / r2-ch14y \u2014 chat 102's computable and prose batches", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/HANDOFF-54.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "recovered_handoff_54_ruling_41", "label": "Ruling 41 \u2014 executed carried state is discarded (W-118, not W-107)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "recovered/HANDOFF-54.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "recovered_handoff_54_ruling_45_class", "label": "The Ruling 45 class \u2014 author- and referee-facing sentences in a reader-facing volume", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/HANDOFF-54.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "recovered_handoff_54_chat_67_hold", "label": "The chat-67 full hold", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "recovered/HANDOFF-54.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "No Register entry, correction or TASK 1 until the review closes, which is why findings are banked in WORKING-REGISTER.md instead."}, {"id": "recovered_handoff_54_member_line_numbering", "label": "Line numbers are MEMBER line numbers, never bundle line numbers", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "recovered/HANDOFF-54.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The bundle numbers each line one higher because of its <<<FILE: header, so a carried bundle line number is off by one."}, {"id": "recovered_handoff_54_form_naming_rule", "label": "A handoff naming N sites for a token must name the form each site carries", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "recovered/HANDOFF-54.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Five chats running corrected a count inside documents about not mis-stating counts, and each cause was a form or a base left unnamed beside the number."}, {"id": "recovered_handoff_54_pointer_off_by_one_class", "label": "The pointer-off-by-one class (docket 9)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/HANDOFF-54.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every \u00a7-pointer is resolved to the claim rather than the heading, in every form of the word, because testing one form is what wrongly produced 14r-22."}, {"id": "recovered_handoff_54_unprinted_input_class", "label": "The unprinted-input class (docket 10)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/HANDOFF-54.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "R3 splits it into conventions unstated and inputs absent; the two are repaired differently."}, {"id": "recovered_handoff_54_single_witness_class", "label": "The single-witness class (docket 17)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/HANDOFF-54.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "R4 should state which figures are unverifiable rather than leaving them looking checked, and distinguish unverifiable from uncorroborated."}, {"id": "recovered_handoff_54_retired_basis_class", "label": "The retired-basis class (docket 15)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/HANDOFF-54.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "recovered_handoff_54_false_universal_class", "label": "The false-universal class (docket 19)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/HANDOFF-54.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A sentence of the form 'every X in this work\u2026' is a computable claim about the collection, not a summary, and is measured against the channel table."}, {"id": "recovered_handoff_54_absent_member_class", "label": "The absent-member class (docket 20)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/HANDOFF-54.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "recovered_handoff_54_heading_only_class", "label": "\u00a714.5.2\u2013\u00a714.5.7 \u2014 six heading-only sections, forty citations (docket 1)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/HANDOFF-54.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Measured against Prints & Proofs as an authoring gap, not a production loss, so R3 authors to the citations that already exist."}, {"id": "recovered_handoff_54_truncation_equality_class", "label": "The truncation-printed-as-equality class (docket 12)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/HANDOFF-54.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "recovered_handoff_54_instrument_suspect_rule", "label": "When an instrument disagrees with a hand reading or the source's own totals line, the instrument is wrong until proved otherwise", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "recovered/HANDOFF-54.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "It fired in every chat from 94 onward; suspecting the book first turns instrument faults into false records."}, {"id": "recovered_handoff_54_working_register", "label": "WORKING-REGISTER.md \u2014 the W- entries (W-101\